{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"e11c3bef-3b37-47fe-a078-3380a15cf81d","agentId":"a058676b8e5461ac3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"You are a skeptical, READ-ONLY code reviewer (write nothing: no files, no git changes; never kill processes by pattern). Review `git -C /home/sauyon/devel/dotfiles/.drovr/wt/orca-cli-skills diff origin/master..HEAD` in full (orca.nix, tests/orca-cli-skills.sh, tests/sandbox-fonts.sh). Angles: security, quality/consistency, comment accuracy (every comment in orca.nix and the test vs the code as it stands — many were rewritten across rounds), test validity (each case fails on a regression of its claim; works with and without a tty; CI viability per .forgejo/workflows/nix-eval.yml — no python3, no util-linux). Round 8; `git log origin/master..HEAD` records earlier fixes and documented accepted limitations — do not re-raise those unless you can show they are actually Important.\n\nContext: public home-manager dotfiles repo (no email addresses or private data). orca.nix packages the Orca Electron AppImage: GUI `orca-ide-app`, CLI `orca-ide`/`orca`, both behind a `forwardSignals` shell launcher; six Orca skills in ~/.claude/skills. master was merged in twice (keybinding work); check the merged orca.nix reads coherently. Confirm the test never prints secret env values (ORCA_AGENT_HOOK_TOKEN is in env) and cleans up its temp dir and background processes (including any left by a failing case).\n\nRate every finding Critical / Important / nit with file:line; say explicitly when none at a severity. Final message = findings."},"uuid":"88c3f3dd-61ae-41a9-b402-a7ba62856175","timestamp":"2026-10-24T12:29:20.455Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/sauyon/devel/dotfiles/.drovr/wt/orca-cli-skills","sessionId":"d19ff9ff-38c8-4378-ac54-4f4061f74300","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"orca-cli-skills"}
